WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.467
-President Trump's former
secretary of defense said,

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.501
in a book and interview,

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.400
that Trump wanted
to shoot protesters

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.067
and called his own
senior officials,

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.834
including
Vice President Mike Pence,

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:11.167
effing losers.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.534
Meanwhile,
the committee investigating

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.767
the January 6th insurrection
is considering whether

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.801
to hold Rudy Giuliani
in contempt

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:18.534
for pulling out
of a scheduled interview.

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.634
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:24.667
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:27.067
So, it seems there are two kinds

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.601
of former Trump associates
who emerge every day.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.501
The first is someone like former
Defense Secretary Mark Esper,

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:33.934
who was on "60 Minutes"
last night

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.000
and who wants you to think

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.467
he stayed
in the Trump administration

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.133
as a check
on Trump's worst instincts.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:40.634
But, now that he has
a book to promote,

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.767
he's willing to tell you
exactly how bad it was.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.968
The other kind are people
like Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:48.000
They don't have books to promote
because they are open books,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.400
telling you everything
about themselves

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.400
and every waking moment.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.534
Rudy is like
a human pop-up book,

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:55.367
[ Laughter ]
the kind you return
to the store

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.801
because it gave
your kid nightmares.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:00.133
Should be noted, if Rudy was
a kid's book character,

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.734
he would be
a reverse Cinderella.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.334
He used to be known
as America's Mayor

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.067
and, now,
you wouldn't be surprised

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:07.067
to see him trying to drive
a giant pumpkin.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.133
[ As Giuliani ]
It won't start.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:11.067
I think the seeds are
in the engine.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.167
I feel comfortable saying

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:16.067
Rudy is the weirdest man
in the history of politics.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.901
Last week,
he posted a video of himself

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:19.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:19.901
on the golf course,

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.234
swinging a club back and forth,

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:24.734
wearing what were either pants
he stole from Gap Kids

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.734
or shorts he stole
from Big &amp; Tall.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.667
[ As Giuliani ]
The great thing about these
pants is they're perfect

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.200
for zero occasions.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.367
It just seems like there are no
ways those pants aren't medical.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.267
The saleslady were like,
"They're very stylish

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.767
and they release Lipitor
right into your bloodstream."

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.000
Then there's the fact he just
keeps swinging the club

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.901
back and forth.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.934
He looks like a great-,
great-, great-,

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.501
great-,
great-grandfather clock.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.834
Anyway, the point is
he's a weird dude

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.667
and, yet, he does not seem,
in any way, aware

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.100
of his weirdness or the
perception of him as a weirdo.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.434
For example, Rudy pulled out
of a scheduled interview

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:07.033
with the committee investigating
the January 6th insurrection

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.434
and he did it
for a typically weird reason.

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.167
-Former Trump attorney
Rudy Giuliani

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.534
has backed out
of an appearance

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.534
before the
January 6th Committee.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.100
He was supposed to take part
in an interview today,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.467
but a spokesman
for the panel said

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:21.100
Giuliani is now refusing
to participate,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.367
unless he is permitted
to record the interview.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:25.067
[ Laughter ]
-Why does he want to record
the interview?

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:26.834
Is he worried they're going to
cut it together

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:27.801
to make it sound bad?

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:28.801
That's what his brain

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.300
already does to his mouth.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.701
What do guys like Rudy always
have Some weird angle,

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.767
like thinking they're
a genius chess master

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.200
calling their bluff
by asking to record the meeting,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.934
but anytime Rudy
has ever been recorded,

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:42.167
it's always been bad for him.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:43.567
He was recorded calling
a senator

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:44.534
on the day of the insurrection,

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:45.634
to get him
to overturn the results.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.767
He was recorded butt-dialing
a reporter

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.467
and talking about how
he needs cash

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.133
as part
of some mysterious plan.

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.767
And he was recorded
by a world-renowned

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.000
investigative reporter,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.200
better known as Borat.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
Rudy records himself

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.067
saying incriminating things
all the time.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:03.934
Before he talks to anyone,
he should pat himself down

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:06.968
to make sure he's not
wearing a wire.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:09.033
[ As Giuliani ]
Check him, to make sure
he's not wearing anything.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.000
"He's clean, boss."

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.133
[ As Giuliani ]
Now, check me.

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.133
"Uh, not good, boss.
You're wearing two wires

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.534
and you have an open voice memo
recording on your phone."

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.634
[ As Giuliani ]
Oh, Rudy, you done it again!

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.400
After he pulled out, Rudy went
on Steve Bannon's podcast

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.701
to explain his decision

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.467
and did not do himself
any favors.

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:27.901
-Are you saying your concern is
they would doctor the tape

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:30.567
and hold it back?
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:31.367
-You want --

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:32.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:35.567
-Come on!

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.501
This is not --
This is not your first ro--

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.100
This is not your first rodeo.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.834
-You got a bunch of people
on that committee

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:43.467
that tried to frame the sitting
president of the United States,

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:45.267
and I'm going to trust them?

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:46.701
Do I look like a fool?

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:49.868
[ Laughter ]
-[ Measuredly ] Do you look like

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:51.601
a fool?

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:54.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.534
Well...

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:56.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.968
♪♪

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:00.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:09.434
♪♪

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:18.868
♪♪

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.601
We've used that last photo
so often,

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:22.968
I've started keeping one in my
wallet now for emergencies.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:25.033
There he goes.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:28.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:33.334
It's fun when I say, "You want
to see a picture of my son?

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:35.534
Aah!"

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.767
Anyway, the important point is,

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.701
now that Rudy is refusing
to testify,

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:44.801
the committee is threatening
to hold him in contempt.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:47.300
-Giuliani's decision
to stonewall the committee

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.868
now puts him on the very same
path as other Trump allies,

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:54.667
like Mark Meadows,
Dan Scavino, and Steve Bannon.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.901
The panel today
dangling the prospect

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.434
of holding Giuliani in contempt,
saying this...

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.234
-Hey, committee, I don't know
how any of this works,

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:17.033
but can you stop waiting
until people don't show up

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:20.601
before you start considering
what their punishment will be?

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:22.634
Why can't you just say,
before they don't show up,

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:23.934
"Either be here
at the appointed time,

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.801
or you're going to jail
and bad news --

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:27.968
they don't have jumpsuits
in your size...

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:29.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.067
...because that's not a size."

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:32.934
It's worth remembering
this guy was

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.267
the president's
personal attorney.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.834
Look, I don't want to put words
in his mouth,

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.901
but I'm starting to think
the people who work for Trump

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:39.968
might be --
and perhaps this is harsh --

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:41.000
effing losers.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.400
-The president is ranting
at the room.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.234
He's using a lot of,
you know, foul language,

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:49.601
you know,
"You all are [effing] losers."

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:50.901
[ Laughter ]
-So that's

00:05:50.901 --> 00:05:52.767
the former Secretary of Defense
Mark Esper.

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.968
You'd be forgiven
for not recognizing him,

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:57.100
since Trump cycled
through more defense secretaries

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.000
than actors
who've played Doctor Who.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.033
[ Laughter ]
Sorry, uh, The Doctor.
I know what it is.

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:03.601
I did it on purpose
to see how many of you

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:04.868
would get your TARDIS
in a twist.

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:06.334
[ Laughter ]
In fact, I guarantee

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.367
at least one person
watching this segment online

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.868
paused the video
as soon as I said that

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:10.801
to write, in all-caps...

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:15.734
[ Laughter ]
And then, when they clicked
Play again

00:06:15.734 --> 00:06:16.934
and saw that
I corrected myself,

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:18.267
they added a follow-up comment
that said...

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:23.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:25.501
Esper was recounting a meeting
in the Oval Office

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:28.567
where Trump suggested
putting active duty troops

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:30.734
in the streets
to suppress lawful protests

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.534
against police brutality
in 2020.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:34.434
And, in the course
of that meeting,

00:06:34.434 --> 00:06:37.133
he apparently looked directly
at his own vice president

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:38.868
and called Mike Pence a loser.

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:42.334
-The president is ranting
at the room.

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:45.167
He's using a lot of,
you know, foul language,

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:48.000
you know, "You all are
[effing] losers," right?

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.968
And then he says it to the
vice president, Mike Pence.

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:53.834
He's using the same language
and he's looking at Pence.

00:06:53.834 --> 00:06:56.400
-He called Mike Pence
an effin' loser?

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.868
-He didn't call him directly,

00:06:57.868 --> 00:07:00.267
but he was looking at him
when he was saying it

00:07:00.267 --> 00:07:01.968
and it really
caught my attention.

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:03.834
-Trump called his aides,
including his own

00:07:03.834 --> 00:07:05.901
vice president, Mike Pence,
[bleep] losers.

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:07.868
I have to imagine
that's when Pence went

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:09.467
into chameleon mode again.

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:11.534
You know that thing he does
where he closes his eyes

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:14.100
[ Laughter ]
and tries to blend
into the background,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.400
hoping to disappear?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.601
It's the same he does
when he's walking in the zoo

00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:19.300
and he sees two monkeys
getting it on.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.868
[ As Pence ]
This isn't happening.

00:07:20.868 --> 00:07:21.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:21.567 --> 00:07:23.300
This isn't happening.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:25.133
They're just wrestling.

00:07:25.133 --> 00:07:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.367 --> 00:07:28.868
They're just wrestling.

00:07:28.868 --> 00:07:30.367
It looks like he's waiting
for Scotty

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:31.367
to beam him out of there.

00:07:31.367 --> 00:07:32.734
[ As Pence ]
This is Commander Pence.

00:07:32.734 --> 00:07:34.067
Away Team is ready.

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:35.167
Energize.

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:39.267
[ Transporter energizing ]
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:42.100
So, why was Trump calling them
[bleep] losers?

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.467
Because they referenced

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:45.467
"Doctor Who" and "Star Trek"
in the same "Closer Look"?

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.267
Surprisingly, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:49.133
He called them losers
because he wanted them

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:52.300
to put active duty troops in the
street to attack protesters

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.334
and they refused,
according to Esper.

00:07:54.334 --> 00:07:57.200
-And I thought that,
"We're in a different spot now.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.834
He's going to finally
give a direct order

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:02.467
to deploy paratroopers

00:08:02.467 --> 00:08:05.200
into the streets
of Washington, D.C.,"

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.334
and I'm thinking
with weapons and bayonets.

00:08:07.334 --> 00:08:09.100
This would be horrible.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.501
-What, specifically,
was he suggesting

00:08:11.501 --> 00:08:15.501
that the U.S. military
should do to these protesters?

00:08:15.501 --> 00:08:18.133
-He says,
"Can't you just shoot them?

00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:20.601
Just shoot them in the legs
or something."

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:22.133
And he's suggesting that
that's what we should do,

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:24.934
that we should bring in the
troops and shoot the protesters.

00:08:24.934 --> 00:08:27.200
-The commander-in-chief
was suggesting

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.400
that the U.S. military
shoot protesters?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.601
-Yes, in the streets

00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:34.334
-American protesters?
-of our nation's capital.

00:08:34.334 --> 00:08:36.300
That's right.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.267
Shocking.

00:08:37.267 --> 00:08:38.667
-It is shocking.
So shocking,

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:40.467
you should've told us
about it at the time.

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:42.100
It's also, somehow,
not surprising to me

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.601
that Trump would specifically
request paratroopers,

00:08:44.601 --> 00:08:46.234
although it also
wouldn't surprise me

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:47.834
if he didn't know
what that word meant.

00:08:47.834 --> 00:08:49.934
I mean, maybe he knows
it's parachutes,

00:08:49.934 --> 00:08:52.667
or maybe he thinks
it's the two guys from "CHiPs."

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:53.801
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ] Ponch and Jon --

00:08:53.801 --> 00:08:56.567
a finer pair of troopers
you'll never see.

00:08:56.567 --> 00:08:58.167
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.167 --> 00:08:59.367
We love Ponch and Jon, don't we?

00:08:59.367 --> 00:09:01.767
The great Erik Estrada.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.767 --> 00:09:03.667
I met him once at a charity
golf tournament

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:05.767
and I said to him,
I said to him, "Erik!

00:09:05.767 --> 00:09:07.334
[ Laughter ]
I love your show,

00:09:07.334 --> 00:09:09.367
but why are there never
any delicious chips?

00:09:09.367 --> 00:09:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.801 --> 00:09:12.334
It seems like
false advertising."

00:09:12.334 --> 00:09:14.234
And he said, "Are you joking?"
I said, "I wish I was, Erik.

00:09:14.234 --> 00:09:15.801
I wish I was, but I'd love --
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.801 --> 00:09:17.534
I'd love to see chips,
if the show is called "CHiPs."

00:09:17.534 --> 00:09:18.901
And he says,
"CHiPs is an acronym,"

00:09:18.901 --> 00:09:20.267
and I just laugh because I don't
know what that word means.

00:09:20.267 --> 00:09:22.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.334 --> 00:09:23.534
I don't know what it means,
so I just laugh.

00:09:23.534 --> 00:09:25.367
I wandered off!

00:09:25.367 --> 00:09:27.167
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.167 --> 00:09:28.801
Trump was an aspiring
authoritarian

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.868
who wanted to use the power
of the state

00:09:30.868 --> 00:09:33.067
to violently suppress dissent
and keep himself in power.

00:09:33.067 --> 00:09:34.968
We don't need any more evidence
to prove that

00:09:34.968 --> 00:09:37.400
these two statements are true,
but we keep getting it, anyway,

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.834
and yet, his closest confidants
are refusing to comply

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:42.334
with the lawful investigation
into Trump's attempted coup.

